## 4. Honesty Framing (mandatory disclaimer block)

> **Absolute-frequency caveat.** The geometry decode yields **dimensionless mode ratios only**. Any Hz value follows entirely from an assumed resonator (size + wave speed + boundary model). We therefore report:
> 1. **Primary:** dimensionless ratios r = f_mode/f_fundamental (resonator-independent).
> 2. **Secondary:** Hz at 2–3 reference resonators as a sensitivity table.

Reference resonators (f₀₁ for circular membrane, radius a: `f₀₁ = (j₀₁/2π)·(c/a)`, j₀₁ = 2.4048):

| Reference resonator | a (m) | c (m/s) | f₀₁ (Hz) | Note | Cents | Comment |
|:--|---:|---:|---:|:--|---:|:--|
| A: 30 cm drumhead | 0.15 | 100 | 255.2 | C4 | −43.3 | mid-audible; physical membrane speeds 50–300 m/s typical |
| B: 30 cm steel plate | 0.15 | ≈1000 (c_eff lumped) | 2 551.6 | D#7 | +43.0 | Chladni-plate regime; plate flexural waves are dispersive — c_eff is mode-dependent, so treat B/C as crude estimates |
| C: 1 m plate | 0.50 | ≈1000 | 765.5 | G5 | −41.4 | |

Additional required statements:
- **Sensitivity:** f ∝ c/a — halving radius or doubling c doubles every frequency (one octave up). State this scaling rule so readers can re-map to any resonator: `f_new = f_ref · (c_new/c_ref)·(a_ref/a_new)`.
- If a claimed "Schumann resonance" or specific Hz target is being matched, the match is only as good as the resonator assumption; a ratio match (JI interval) is a stronger, assumption-free claim than an absolute-Hz match.
- Infrasonic/ultrasonic outputs (likely for large/slow or small/fast resonators) are labeled per §1.2 and are not "musical notes" in the perceptual sense — the note name is a mathematical placement on the 12-TET lattice only.

